If size > 2^62 and capacity overflowed... sizes beyond 4 EiB are impossible in practice (and with signed 64-bit off_t, max is ~8 EiB = 2^63-1, so size in range (2^62, 2^63) does actually exist). For those we need depth 6, capacity 2^72 — doesn't fit in 64 bits, but we just need to stop the loop. Add a bound: if capacity > ULLONG_MAX/TREEDIRSIZE, then one more level is enough for any off_t size (since size < 2^63 < 2^72)... wait, is that really so? capacity=2^62, next is 2^72 > 2^63-1 ≥ size. So:

```c
static int treedepth(off_t size)
{
	int depth = 1;
	unsigned long long capacity = (unsigned long long)TREEDIRSIZE * TREEPAGESIZE;

	while (capacity < (unsigned long long)size) {
