Loop iteration 1: p = strrchr → the '/FILE1023' part → *p=0 → buf="/tmp/.../nbd/TREE1023/TREE1023" → rmdir ✓ → p=strrchr → '/TREE1023' → rmdir ✓ → buf=".../nbd/TREE1023"... continues → rmdir nbd ✓ → buf="/tmp/treefiles-test-XXX" → p = strrchr finds the '/' before "treefiles-test-XXX" → *p=0 → buf="/tmp" → rmdir("/tmp") fails → count_assert fails!!

Bug! The loop has to stop after rmdir-ing the tree's root (nbd). Fix: either track the base length of name, or stop when strlen(buf) <= strlen(root) + ... . The simplest approach: only rmdir as long as strlen(buf) > strlen(root):

